mission "The Wreck of the Saint Oria"
    name "The Wreck of the Saint Oria"
    description "Recover a logbook from the expedition's flagship, wrecked beyond the outer reef."
    source "Port de Lune"
    destination "Wreckers' Moon"
    reward 1785
    speaker offer "Marda Quill"
    speaker visit "Marda Quill"
    speaker complete "Marda Quill"
    to offer
        has "The False Beacon: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The outer reef has given up a section of hull from the Saint Oria. The ship's name is still visible beneath the weed, and the wreck lies beyond the usual salvage grounds.`
            `Marda Quill studies the name on the timber. "The Saint Oria was the expedition's flagship. If her logbook survived, it may tell us why she was sent west and why no official chart admits she was ever there."`
            choice
                `"You can count on my ship. What is the first step?"`
                    accept
                `"Before I agree, tell me what I might be sailing into."`
                    goto details
                `"My crew did not sign on for this kind of trouble."`
                    close
            label details
                `Marda marks the reef on your chart. "The wreck lies beyond the outer reef. The water is not forgiving, so take only what you can recover safely. I want the logbook, not another ship added to the wreck list."`
                choice
                    `"I will do what I can. We should get underway."`
                        accept
                    `"That risk is not mine to take."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Wreck of the Saint Oria. Recover a logbook from the expedition's flagship, wrecked beyond the outer reef."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Wreckers' Moon, Marda examines the logbook's water-stained pages. The entries point to a place deliberately removed from every official chart. "They were sent farther west than the public orders admit," she says. "The log may finally tell us why."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Marda closes the logbook with both hands. "This is the first account from someone aboard the Saint Oria. It deserves to be read, not locked away. We will copy it and let the island councils judge what it means."`
        log "Completed The Wreck of the Saint Oria. Received 1785 gold. Recover a logbook from the expedition's flagship, wrecked beyond the outer reef."
